    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds **ADR-059: Selector index for cascade performance**. **Documentation only.** Implementation (~250 lines across 4 source files) lands in a follow-up PR.\n\nTargets the 1058ms cascade phase that ADR-058's split-timer measured. Expected win: cascade → under 300ms (3.5×+), total Wikipedia render → ~2.4s.\n\n## The measurement driving this\n\n**ADR-058's split-timer, Release build, Wikipedia HTML article:**\n\n```\nPERF-CASCADE: 1057.9ms  PERF-LAYOUT: 2379.3ms  PERF-TOTAL: 3437.2ms\n```\n\nCascade is **31%** of the total. Layout is 69% (ADR-060 territory).\n\n## What the current cascade does\n\nPer element × 3 pseudo-targets (None, Before, After):\n\n```\nfor each rule in ua_sheet.rules:   apply_rule\nfor each rule in author_sheet.rules: apply_rule\n```\n\n**Wikipedia:** ~5000 elements × ~2000 rules × 3 pseudo targets ≈ **30 million `apply_rule` invocations** per page load. Each does full selector matching from the rightmost compound backward.\n\n## The indexing invariant\n\n**For a rule to match an element, every simple selector in the rightmost compound must match.**\n\n- Rightmost compound has `#foo` → element must have `id=\"foo\"`\n- Has `.bar` → element must have class `bar`\n- Has `div` → element must be `<div>`\n\nSo we bucket rules by the **most selective rightmost simple** and query only plausible candidates:\n\n| Bucket | Rules indexed by | Size (typical) |\n|---|---|---|\n| **by_id** | `SimpleKind::Id` name | Tiny (usually 0–1) |\n| **by_class** | `SimpleKind::Class` name | Small (0–20 per class) |\n| **by_type** | `SimpleKind::Type` name | Medium (10–50) |\n| **universal** | `*`, `[attr]`, `:root`, `:hover` | Large (100–1000) |\n\n**Query per element** = id bucket + all class buckets + type bucket + universal bucket. Union = candidates.\n\n**Typical element:** ~100 candidates vs ~2000 all rules = **20× reduction**.\n\n## What exists that supports this\n\n`SimpleSelector` (selectors.hpp:84) has typed `SimpleKind` enum — `Type`, `Class`, `Id`, `Universal`, etc. `name` field holds the class/id/tag. `CompoundSelector` holds `vector<SimpleSelector>`. Clean structure for indexing.\n\n`Selector::matches` (selectors.cpp:869-882) already extracts pseudo-element from the rightmost compound and filters on `target`. **Index doesn't need pseudo partitioning** — `matches()` handles it.\n\n## Design decisions\n\n### Bucket by most selective simple (ID > Class > Type > Universal)\n\nMultiple classes in one compound (`.a.b`): index by first (deterministic). Any \"must-match\" simple preserves the invariant — we pick the most selective for bucket size.\n\n### Unified index (no pseudo-target partitioning)\n\n3× faster query, 3× memory. Waste is ~33 fast-fail pseudo checks per element per pass × 5000 = ~5ms. Negligible. Ship unified.\n\n### Build at parse time; rules not mutated post-parse\n\n`std::vector` move preserves element addresses, so `Rule*` in index survives `Stylesheet` move-return. Documented invariant: callers don't mutate `rules` after `parse()`. Holds today (cascade takes `const Stylesheet&`).\n\n### Dedupe via sort+unique by pointer\n\nMulti-selector rules land in multiple buckets. Sort + unique on ~50 candidates = ~300 comparisons. Trivial. Alternative hash-set allocates more.\n\n### Reuse candidates across 3 pseudo-target passes\n\nCompute candidates once per element, iterate 3× (once per pseudo). `matches()` filters pseudo-target internally.\n\n## The 3 regression concerns (documented in spec)\n\n1. **`apply_rule_call_count` tests** (3 sites in test_layout.cpp) — counter drops from ~thousands to ~tens. Tests need revision or relative assertions.\n2. **Universal-bucket rules** — `:root`, `[attr]`, `*` fall into universal, queried per element. Correctness preserved, but no savings if a stylesheet has ~1000 such rules.\n3. **Order within bucket** may reorder (pointer sort). Cascade specificity resolution is order-independent; trace assertions may need update.\n\n**All three are caught by the existing 125 test_stylesheet.cpp tests** — they cover selector variants, cascade ordering, specificity. Any break is a real bug, not expected flip.\n\n## Deferred (documented)\n\n- Pseudo-target partitioning (3× memory, not needed)\n- `[attribute]` indexing (rare, universal-bucketed)\n- Descendant combinator ancestor pre-filtering\n- **Layout's 2379ms** — ADR-060 territory\n\n## Test count target\n\n- 675 → ~680 (+5 new tests, 3 counter tests may flip)\n\n## Success criterion\n\n**`PERF-CASCADE < 300ms`** (3.5× minimum win) on Wikipedia Release build. If > 300ms, the index is ineffective (likely too many universal-bucket rules) — investigate before shipping.\n\n**`PERF-TOTAL` drop**: 3437ms → ~2400ms (cascade saves ~860ms; layout unchanged).\n\nRefs #257\n",
